WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
A map grid, where each
square is one kilometre.

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.350
Village A sits at one, two.

3
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.260
Village B sits at seven, six.

4
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:13.860
A phone mast must stand exactly the
same distance from both villages.

5
00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.910
The halfway point, four,
four, clearly works.

6
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.990
But is that the only spot?

7
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.150
Could the mast stand anywhere else?

8
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.050
And if so, where?

9
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.140
In this mission, you'll find
the midpoint of a line segment,

10
00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:29.080
and the gradient of the
line through two points.

11
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.450
You'll find the gradient
of a perpendicular line,

12
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.440
using the negative reciprocal.

13
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:39.060
And you'll write a straight line's
equation in the form a x plus b y equals c.

14
00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: find where
the mast can stand,

15
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.670
so that it is equally
far from both villages.
